From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:20:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mailbox: apple,mailbox: Add
 apple,hold-rx-in-sleep

Some coprocessors message the AP periodically while idle: the J713's
GPU firmware asks for ring service about twice a second, and its AOP
sends a report every second. Describe a mailbox whose messages need not
wake the system, so the OS can leave them in the FIFO while it sleeps
and handle them at resume.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 36743381282d9b9319c65571858ec8bc63fe6955)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml         | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
index 7e7644c173..04fbc40f01 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mailbox/apple,mailbox.yaml
@@ -112,6 +112,13 @@ properties:
   resets:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  apple,hold-rx-in-sleep:
+    description:
+      Messages from this coprocessor need not wake the system. The OS may
+      leave them in the receive FIFO while the system sleeps and handle
+      them at resume.
+    type: boolean
+
   power-domains:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
